+\item \textbf{\sys{} works with or without a model-built memory.}
+The original implementation combines evidence from model-built memories and raw text (Section~\ref{sec:beamscale}). We number Mem0's memories one per line in write order, so detection reads them as a numbered log, and a team that runs Mem0 can keep its store. \sys{} reads them beside the conversation under one budget and averages $73.1$ on BEAM, above either store alone ($70.8$ to $72.0$) and every system at that budget.
